## Example API Calls

### Example 1: Payment Exceeds Due
```javascript
// Customer has PKR 1,000 due, pays PKR 1,500
POST /api/customers/1/payments
{
  "type": "payment",
  "amount": 1500.00,
  "description": "Payment received"
}

// Result:
// - Due: PKR 0 (1,000 paid off)
// - Advance: PKR 500 (excess becomes advance)
```

### Example 2: Customer Has Due, Pays "Advance" Type Payment
```javascript
// Customer has PKR 1,000 due, pays PKR 800 as "advance"
POST /api/customers/1/payments
{
  "type": "advance",
  "amount": 800.00,
  "description": "Advance payment"
}

// Result:
// - Due: PKR 200 (1,000 - 800, due paid first)
// - Advance: PKR 0 (no excess because 800 < 1,000)
```

### Example 3: Customer Has Due, Pays Large "Advance" Payment
```javascript
// Customer has PKR 1,000 due, pays PKR 1,500 as "advance"
POST /api/customers/1/payments
{
  "type": "advance",
  "amount": 1500.00,
  "description": "Advance payment"
}

// Result:
// - Due: PKR 0 (1,000 paid off completely)
// - Advance: PKR 500 (excess: 1,500 - 1,000 becomes advance)
```

**Note:** Even though the payment type is "advance", it still pays off due balance first!

